[32m+[m[32m## OpenTelemetry[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mInstall the optional adapter:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```bash[m
[32m+[m[32mpip install "modelcore[otel]"[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mYour application remains responsible for configuring its own OpenTelemetry tracer provider and exporter. ModelCore neither configures global telemetry nor requires a collector:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```python[m
[32m+[m[32mfrom opentelemetry import trace[m
[32m+[m[32mfrom modelcore.application import TelemetryProvider[m
[32m+[m[32mfrom modelcore.telemetry.opentelemetry import OpenTelemetrySink[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mtracer = trace.get_tracer("my_application.modelcore")[m
[32m+[m[32mobserved = TelemetryProvider(provider, OpenTelemetrySink(tracer))[m
[32m+[m[32mresponse = await observed.generate(request)[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe adapter emits one `modelcore.generate` span for a completed normal generation. It includes safe operational metadata (provider, model, duration, success, token usage, and safe error type); it never includes prompts, messages, generated content, tool payloads, credentials, or raw exception text.[m
